{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass, when Elohim destroyed.</b> This is the angel. <b>And Elohim remembered Abraham.</b> This is the Holy One, blessed be He. <b>And He sent Lot.</b> Through the remembrance of Abraham He saved those who cleave to him. And the explanation of the matter is that were it not for Abraham, Lot would still have been in Haran, which is his land and his birthplace; but for the honor of Abraham he went forth with him, as the verse says (Genesis 12:4): ״וילך אברם כאשר דבר אליו ה׳ וילך אתו לוט״. Therefore Scripture mentions that through the remembrance of Abraham Lot was saved with him, and this is what our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: one saves the case of the scroll together with the scroll, and the case of the tefillin together with the tefillin — and even if there were coins inside the case, one saves it for the honor of the scroll or for the honor of the tefillin. To teach you: fortunate are the righteous and fortunate are those who cleave to them. And so we find with Noah the righteous (Genesis 8:1): ״ויזכר אלהים את נח ואת כל החיה ואת כל הבהמה אשר אתו בתבה״." "<b>In the overturning of the cities wherein Lot dwelt.</b> One should ask: this overturning and this great judgment upon Sodom — why? For there were certainly nations in the world that were as evil and sinful as they were, yet the punishment upon them was not so severe; and furthermore, Abraham, who was the root of the faith, could have brought them back in repentance, and repentance outweighs everything. But because the city of Sodom was part of the land of Israel, therefore this judgment was so great, on account of the merit of the Holy Land, which does not tolerate transgressors — and it would vomit out those men of abomination; and therefore it vomited out this nation from there beforehand." "<b>And behold,</b> this matter of the overturning of Sodom was a sign and a token for Israel, who were destined to inherit it, that if they are not careful with the inheritance of the land through observance of the Torah and the commandments, it will vomit them out from it, just as it vomited out the men of Sodom beforehand, and just as it vomited out the men of the Canaanites after them. And so Moses our teacher, peace be upon him, mentioned at the end of his days, and he reminded them of the destruction of Sodom, and said that the land would vomit out if Israel abandons the Torah, and that is His saying (Deuteronomy 29:22): ״גפרית ומלח שרפה כל ארצה״ and so on, ״כמהפכת סדום ועמורה״ and so on, ״על מה עשה ה׳ ככה״ and so on, ״על אשר עזבו״ and so on."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:47.481289332Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}